# CODEOWNERS — risk-tiered human review.
# See docs/vv-master-plan.txt section 5c.
#
# Philosophy: CI is the gate for the common path; a human reviewer is REQUIRED
# only on HIGH-RISK paths. There is intentionally NO `*` default line — most PRs
# are gated by CI + the lead owner's curation, not a blocking review, so the
# one-owner/one-branch/one-PR flow stays fast.
#
# ENFORCEMENT: these rules only block a merge if branch protection on `main` has
# "Require review from Code Owners" enabled. With that on, the automerge workflow
# (which merges via GITHUB_TOKEN and cannot approve) will NOT be able to land a
# high-risk PR until a listed owner approves — which is exactly the intent.
# An author cannot approve their own PR, so high-risk changes always get a second
# set of eyes.

